   "he": "וּשְׁתֵּי הַלֶּחֶם וּשְׁנֵי כִּבְשֵׂי עֲצֶרֶת [וְכוּ׳]. תָּנוּ רַבָּנַן: ״וְהֵנִיף הַכֹּהֵן אֹתָם עַל לֶחֶם הַבִּיכּוּרִים״,",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: «And the two loaves and» the accompanying peace offering of «two lambs» brought on «Shavuot» also require waving. With regard to this waving, «the Sages taught» in a baraita: The verse states: «“And the priest shall wave them upon the bread of the first fruits» for a wave offering before the Lord, upon the two lambs; they shall be holy to the Lord for the priest” (Leviticus 23:20)."
